# Verible lint rule set for this core.
#
# Waived rules are convention mismatches, not defects -- each is disabled for a
# stated reason rather than because it was noisy.

# Verible's default constant regex rejects underscores, which would flag every
# ALL_CAPS ISA constant (OPC_LOAD, F3_SB, REG_COUNT). ALL_CAPS_WITH_UNDERSCORES
# is the convention for opcode/funct fields and is what this project uses.
-parameter-name-style

# Wants `mem [N]` instead of `mem [0:N-1]`. Equivalent, and the explicit range
# documents the direction -- which matters here because instr_mem, data_mem and
# reg_file are all $readmemh targets, and $readmemh fills left index first.
-unpacked-dimensions-range-ordering

# Enforcing a column limit here would mean reflowing lines whose only fault is a
# long trailing comment, which is churn on working RTL for no defect caught.
# Long lines that hid a real problem (the duplicated forwarding predicate in
# cpu_core) were fixed by naming the subexpression, not by wrapping them.
-line-length
